[32.14163, "i", "tigris buckets --help\n"]
[32.14194, "o", "tigris buckets --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[32.305401, "o", "Usage: tigris buckets|b [options] [command]\r\n\r\nCreate, inspect, update, and delete buckets. Buckets are top-level containers that hold objects\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -h, --help                          display help for command\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  list|l [options]                    List all buckets in the current organization\r\n  create|c [options] [name]           Create a new bucket with optional access, tier, and location settings\r\n  rebase [options] <fork>             Update a fork with the latest changes from its source bucket\r\n  merge [options] <fork>              Merge a fork's changes back into its source bucket\r\n  get|g [options] <name>              Show details for a bucket including access level, region, tier, and custom domain\r\n  delete|d [options] <name>           Delete one or more buckets by name. The bucket must be empty or delete-protection must be off\r\n  restore [options] <name>            Restore a soft-deleted bucket within its retention window. List recoverable buckets with \"tigris buckets list --deleted\"\r\n  set|s [options] <name>              Update settings on an existing bucket such as access level, location, caching, or custom domain\r\n  enable-snapshots [options] <name>   Enable snapshots on an existing bucket, converting it to a snapshot bucket\r\n  disable-snapshots [options] <name>  Disable snapshots on an existing bucket, converting it back to a regular bucket. Rejected while the bucket has dependent\r\n                                      forks\r\n  set-locations [options] <name>      Set the data locations for a bucket\r\n  set-migration [options] <name>      Configure data migration from an external S3-compatible source bucket. Tigris will pull objects on demand from the source\r\n  migrate [options] <path>            Actively migrate all objects from a shadow bucket to Tigris by scheduling server-side migration for unmigrated objects\r\n  lifecycle|lc                        Manage bucket lifecycle rules. Each rule combines an optional storage-class transition and/or expiration (TTL), scoped to\r\n                                      an optional key prefix\r\n  set-notifications [options] <name>  Configure object event notifications on a bucket. Sends webhook requests to a URL when objects are created, updated, or\r\n                                      deleted\r\n  set-cors [options] <name>           Configure CORS rules on a bucket. Each invocation adds a rule unless --override or --reset is used\r\n  help                                Show help for this command\r\n"]
[32.31095, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@bc986082-8e1c-4e44-bb65-6ed63b12cd1b:~# "]
[35.350269, "i", "tigris buckets lifecycle --help\n"]
[35.350691, "o", "tigris buckets lifecycle --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[35.512031, "o", "Usage: tigris buckets lifecycle|lc [options] [command]\r\n\r\nManage bucket lifecycle rules. Each rule combines an optional storage-class transition and/or expiration (TTL), scoped to an optional key prefix\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -h, --help                    display help for command\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  list|l [options] <name>       List lifecycle rules on a bucket\r\n  create|c [options] <name>     Create a new lifecycle rule. A rule must include a transition (--storage-class with --days or --date) and/or an expiration\r\n                                (--expire-days or --expire-date), and may optionally be scoped via --prefix\r\n  edit|e [options] <name> <id>  Edit an existing lifecycle rule by its id. Only specified fields are changed\r\n  help                          Show help for this command\r\n"]
[35.517513, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@bc986082-8e1c-4e44-bb65-6ed63b12cd1b:~# "]
[38.404957, "i", "tigris buckets lifecycle create --help\n"]
[38.405463, "o", "tigris buckets lifecycle create --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[38.606062, "o", "Usage: tigris buckets lifecycle create|c [options] [command] <name>\r\n\r\nCreate a new lifecycle rule. A rule must include a transition (--storage-class with --days or --date) and/or an expiration (--expire-days or --expire-date), and\r\nmay optionally be scoped via --prefix\r\n\r\nArguments:\r\n  name                         Name of the bucket\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  -p, --prefix [value]         Key prefix to scope the rule to. Omit for a bucket-wide rule\r\n  -s, --storage-class <value>  Target storage class for the transition\r\n  -d, --days [value]           Transition objects after this many days (used with --storage-class)\r\n  --date [value]               Transition objects on this date (ISO-8601, e.g. 2026-06-01) (used with --storage-class)\r\n  --expire-days [value]        Expire (delete) objects after this many days\r\n  --expire-date [value]        Expire (delete) objects on this date (ISO-8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)\r\n  --disable                    Create the rule in a disabled state\r\n  --format <value>             Output format (default: \"table\")\r\n  --json                       Output as JSON\r\n  -y, --yes                    Skip confirmation prompts\r\n  -h, --help                   display help for command\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  help                         Show help for this command\r\n"]
[38.612011, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@bc986082-8e1c-4e44-bb65-6ed63b12cd1b:~# "]
[41.295279, "i", "tigris buckets lifecycle create \"$BUCKET\" --expire-days 7 -y\n"]
[41.295764, "o", "tigris buckets lifecycle create \"$BUCKET\" --expire-days 7 -y\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[41.653761, "o", "Creating lifecycle rule...\r\n"]
[42.032696, "o", "✖ Failed to create lifecycle rule\r\n  Lifecycle rules and expiration are not supported for buckets with versioning enabled or converted from versioned\r\n"]
[42.046407, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@bc986082-8e1c-4e44-bb65-6ed63b12cd1b:~# "]
[47.709262, "i", "tigris buckets set --help\n"]
[47.709707, "o", "tigris buckets set --help\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[47.837363, "o", "Usage: tigris buckets set|s [options] [command] <name>\r\n\r\nUpdate settings on an existing bucket such as access level, location, caching, or custom domain\r\n\r\nArguments:\r\n  name                                 Name of the bucket\r\n\r\nOptions:\r\n  --access <value>                     Bucket access level\r\n  --locations <value>                  Bucket location (see https://www.tigrisdata.com/docs/buckets/locations/ for more details)\r\n  --allow-object-acl [value]           Enable object-level ACL\r\n  --disable-directory-listing [value]  Disable directory listing\r\n  --cache-control [value]              Default cache-control header value\r\n  --custom-domain [value]              Custom domain for the bucket\r\n  --enable-delete-protection [value]   (deprecated) Enable delete protection Use --soft-delete instead.\r\n  --soft-delete <value>                Enable or disable soft delete (recoverable deletes). Requires --retention-days when enabling\r\n  --retention-days [value]             Number of days to retain soft-deleted objects (required when enabling --soft-delete)\r\n  --enable-additional-headers [value]  Enable additional HTTP headers (X-Content-Type-Options nosniff)\r\n  --format <value>                     Output format (default: \"table\")\r\n  --json                               Output as JSON\r\n  -y, --yes                            Skip confirmation prompts\r\n  -h, --help                           display help for command\r\n\r\nCommands:\r\n  help                                 Show help for this command\r\n"]
[47.842943, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
